{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Patch set 1 of Gerrit 3160 (pytest 9.2.0) got LLM-Review +1 but Verified -1 (run 41137997776). Both failures come from 9.2.0 itself, not from the #14635 fix:\n1. 6 review-bot tests: AttributeError 'State' object has no attribute 'config'. Reproduced locally: on 9.1.1 the 3 test files pass (142 passed); on 9.2.0 3 fail. 9.2.0's MonkeyPatch.setattr records the old value from __dict__, so undo DELETES starlette State attributes (a 4-line script confirmed it: after undo, app.state.config is missing). Upstream pytest-dev/pytest#15099, still open.\n2. Mutation gate, every shard: mutmut 3.7.0 crashes in its stats hook on item._nodeid, which 9.2.0 removed (boxed/mutmut#615, fixed in mutmut 3.8.1). Reproduced locally with scripts/mutation_gate.py run --shard signing.\nPatch set 2 locks pytest 9.0.3 instead (newest release without #14635; constraint still excludes 9.1.0/9.1.1). On 9.0.3: regression test passes; orchestrate items keep the conftest fixtures (collect probe True 235); the Observation's -n 4 command plus the regression and review-bot tests: 2265 passed, 13 skipped, exit 0 (run5); full default-suite collection succeeds (20087 collected); local mutation gate gets past the stats phase (stats written, mutant testing started; stopped there to save host time). make lint passes.\nAdopting 9.2.0 is filed as zodiacal-rockbound-egret (discovered_from this ticket); it needs the review-bot monkeypatch change or the upstream #15099 fix, and a measured mutmut upgrade."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793404329952728001,"uuid":"ea5145b0-5d8d-4781-8585-0df1040df80c"}